   "note": "Estimate, not a survey. The Richmond-Petersburg Turnpike (1955-58) and its later ramps cut a trench up to about 9 m deep through the ward and raised fills at the junction above Shockoe Valley. Inside this outline the lidar is set aside: the outline is today's motorway and ramp ways (OSM) buffered 22 m (10 m for ramps), widened over the cut and fill slopes the lidar shows (slopes over 12% within 60 m of a motorway), then simplified; the I-64 viaduct over the valley is left out, its ground kept as measured. The ground inside is rebuilt as the smoothest surface (a membrane) that meets the measured ground at the outline and runs each street listed here through at grade, straight between its surviving ends. Checked against the USGS Richmond 1:24,000 sheet surveyed 1933-34 (10-foot contours; see ground.md in the story folder for the comparison and the error estimate).",
   "sources": [
    "https://apps.nationalmap.gov/3depdem/",
